      "sourceLink": null,
      "spam": false,
      "statusChangeID": null,
      "value": "Or they could copy NeosVR and just add multiple locomotion options to our menus that world creators control. You want to let people fly in your map? Check the checkbox, and they can use their hand menu to turn it on. It really feels like VRChat has done nothing but take features away and work on systems to \"optimize\" for 2 years now. The biggest achievement in socializing was getting avatar chairs (which was initially a mistake, eventually implemented purposefully), and the other was the climbing system made by some guy inspired by (you guessed it) NeosVR.",
